cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Value-Field Theory (VFT)"
message: "If you use this theory or repository, please cite this repository."
authors:
  - family-names: "Nuno"
    given-names: "T."
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
abstract: >
  Value-Field Theory (VFT) is a structural framework and common state
  representation for describing how a shared multidimensional real-resource
  world K, actor-specific access and usability views K_i, and actor-specific
  subjective evaluation and expectation states P_i condition actor-side
  processes and events A_i. K_i is not required to be a set-theoretic subset
  of K; it is a derived actor-relative access, usability, exercisability, or
  referenceability view of the shared resource world. For another actor a,
  P_j(a) denotes actor j's evaluation, belief, credit assessment, or expectation
  about a, rather than a state held by a. Delta K(S,tau) is reserved for a
  specification-indexed state or resource change descriptor. In general,
  Y_S(t)=M_S(K_t) and Delta K(S,tau)=delta_S(Y_S(t0),Y_S(t1)) in D_S, where the
  change operator need not be an arithmetic difference. Gross production,
  consumption, transaction volume, transformation, and other interval activity
  statistics are not folded into Delta K; when needed they are represented by
  projection-local derived path functionals such as H_S(tau). Where an
  expectation is defined, a quantitative representation q_S:D_S->V_S is
  specified and E_i[Delta K(S,tau)] is shorthand for the expectation of
  q_S(Delta K(S,tau)). Delta P_i is likewise a change descriptor or state
  transition and need not be an arithmetic difference. Planned or chosen
  resource changes are distinct from forecasts and may be represented by
  projection-local variables such as x_i. Economic budget feasibility,
  inter-agent compatibility, market-equilibrium conditions, accounting
  identities, surplus, decentralized adjustment, micro-macro linkages, and
  reputation- or credit-economy models are domain-specific projection
  candidates rather than universal consequences of the VFT Core. VFT does not
  fix a universal probability measure, expectation-formation equation,
  action-selection rule, state-transition law, compatibility condition,
  market-equilibrium condition, or aggregation law.
repository-code: "https://github.com/nuno929/vf-model"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
